'''visual''' (viz̮′ū-al), ''a.'' [< OF. ''visual'', ''visuel'', F. ''visuel'' = Sp. Pg. ''visual'' = It. ''visuale'', < LL. ''visualis'', of sight, < L. ''visus'', sight, < ''videre'', pp. ''visus'', see: see ''vis''<sup>1</sup>, ''visage''.] '''1.''' Of or pertaining to sight; relating to vision; used in sight; serving as the instrument of seeing; optic: as, the ''visual'' nerve.

{{smaller block|<poem>The air,
No where so clear, sharpen’d his ''visual'' ray.</poem>
{{right|''Milton'', P. L., iii. 620.}}}}

{{smaller block|''Visual'' perception sees a superficies, but it does not see a superficies as distinguished from a solid.
